From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VIctory contributor <contributor@users.noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 17:12:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 12/43] Shaders: a sampler used with and without comparison
 gets two slots

Static sampler slots were deduplicated by the four sampler words alone.
The same words used for an ordinary sample and a comparison sample
shared a slot, and the comparison use marked it as a comparison one:
the ordinary sample then got a comparison handle (or, met in the other
order, a handle and slot metadata that disagreed). The DXIL validator
requires the sampler kind to match the operation.

A slot is now chosen by the words and whether the use compares, so the
two ways get their own slots, and the slot's kind is fixed at its first
use instead of folded into a bitfield later. The comparison bit moves
from the Lowered bitfield into the slot list (its kind travels with it).

AI use: written with Codex and Claude Code (GPT-5.2 Codex); reviewed and
posted with my approval. No game files were used.

(cherry picked from commit 6390a18bce944adef78c99b4fab07c67fb551b14)
(cherry picked from commit cc7b8718f02b442f570448406c933e0a7e1c233b)
